# EtSkeleton Component

## Overview

`EtSkeleton` is the loading-placeholder system. It is built around a **single
app-wide pulse clock**, so a screen full of placeholders costs exactly one
animation loop (not one per shape) and every pulse stays phase-synced.

**Location:** `/libs/etoro-ui/src/components/status/skeleton/`

## Architecture

> Built for the **New Architecture (Fabric)**, where `MaskedView` alpha clipping
> and Reanimated layout animations (`entering`/`exiting`) are both unreliable.
> The system therefore depends on NEITHER: atoms pulse their opacity directly,
> and the dissolve is a shared-value opacity crossfade.

- **Shared clock** (`hooks/use-shimmer-clock.ts`): one module-level `makeMutable`
  progress value driven by a single ref-counted `withRepeat` loop. Every skeleton
  reads it, so all pulses are phase-synced and N skeletons = 1 timing animation.
- **Shape atoms** (`EtSkeleton`, `EtSkeleton.Box`, `EtSkeleton.Circle`,
  `EtSkeleton.Text`): each is a solid base-color shape whose opacity pulses from
  `useShimmerClock()`. There is no gradient layer, travelling sheen, highlight
  token, or transform animation in the shipped model. No `MaskedView`.
- **`EtSkeleton.Group`** (`components/et-skeleton-group-host.tsx`): a pure flexbox
  layout host. It lays atoms out to mirror real content and toggles their shimmer
  for the whole section at once (`animated={false}`). It owns no animation of its
  own.
- **Skeleton↔content transition lives in `EtView` / `EtScrollView`**
  (`components/view/`): the one true skeleton↔content transition is no longer a
  skeleton subcomponent — it is owned by the loading-aware container components.
  Pass `loading` + `skeleton` to an `EtView`/`EtScrollView` and it keeps both
  layers mounted and dissolves the skeleton with a shared-value **opacity**
  animation (reliable on Fabric), then unmounts it. While `loading` the skeleton
  is in normal flow (reserves height); once loaded, `children` mount in flow and
  the skeleton fades out as an `absoluteFill` overlay over them. Works the same in
  a ScrollView, an `EtScreen.View`, a FlashList header, or any conditional branch
  — no per-screen overlays. Honors OS reduce-motion. See `view/AGENTS.md`.
- **`EtSkeleton.Chips`** / `EtSkeletonChips` (`components/et-skeleton-chips.tsx`):
  a preset row of pill placeholders sized to `EtChip` (height 32, radius 20,
  `gap: X2`). Reserve it in the exact slot a filter-chips rail
  (`EtChipsGroupV2` / `EtSection.Chips`) will occupy during load so the chips
  appearing on data-ready don't push the list down. Props: `count?`, `widths?`,
  `style`, `testID`.
- **Theme tokens only**: base = `bgNeutralGreyPrimary`. The pulse changes opacity
  only; never hardcode colors.

## Usage

```tsx
import { EtSkeleton, EtView } from 'etoro-ui';
import { View } from 'react-native';

// Preferred: a Group mirroring the real content, one synchronized shimmer.
<EtSkeleton.Group style={{ gap: 16 }}>
  {rows.map((id) => (
    <View key={id} style={styles.row}>
      <EtSkeleton.Circle width={40} height={40} />
      <View style={{ flex: 1, gap: 8 }}>
        <EtSkeleton.Text width="70%" height={14} />
        <EtSkeleton.Text width="40%" height={12} />
      </View>
    </View>
  ))}
</EtSkeleton.Group>

// Skeleton -> content (EtView dissolves the skeleton, no hard cut)
<EtView loading={isLoading} skeleton={<MySectionSkeleton />}>
  <MySection data={data} />
</EtView>

// Standalone atom (still fine; auto-shimmers off the shared clock)
<EtSkeleton width="60%" height={16} />
```

## Integration standard

1. **Always transition through `EtView` / `EtScrollView`** — never `isLoading ?
   <Skeleton/> : <Content/>` directly. The container owns the dissolve, so it
   fires reliably regardless of the surrounding structure. Do NOT add your own
   `Animated.View` / `FadeIn` / `FadeOut` wrappers or absolute overlays.
2. **Encapsulate loading inside the smart component.** A component that owns its
   UI should take a `loading` prop and render its own `EtView`/`skeleton`
   internally, so parents stay clean (`<MySection loading={isLoading} ... />`).
   Keep the `EtView` at the feature level only when wrapping an unowned kit
   component you cannot push into (e.g. `EtSection.Chips`).
3. **One `EtSkeleton.Group` per section/list body** — not per element.
4. **Shape + height match** the real content; share a height constant between a
   skeleton row and its real row so the swap never jumps.
5. **Keep the scroll owner mounted.** For a FlashList body, wrap the whole body
   (list + its skeleton) in a single `EtView` rather than feeding the list its own
   loading state — the skeleton overlay fades over the mounted list.
6. **Skeleton definitions live in a per-feature `loaders/` folder.** Keep the
   `*-skeleton.tsx` filenames; the smart component imports its skeleton from
   `../loaders/...` so feature files stay free of placeholder markup.
7. Prefer row slots `EtListItemV2.Skeleton` / `EtAssetItem.Skeleton` for list rows.

## Props (`EtSkeleton`)

| Prop | Type | Default | Description |
|------|------|---------|-------------|
| `width` | `number \| string` | `'100%'` | Width of the shape |
| `height` | `number` | `20` | Height of the shape |
| `variant` | `'text' \| 'circular' \| 'rectangular' \| 'rounded'` | `'text'` | Shape / default radius |
| `borderRadius` | `number` | varies | Explicit radius override |
| `animation` | `'shimmer' \| 'none' \| ...` | `'shimmer'` | `'none'` renders a static shape; any other value shimmers |
| `visible` | `boolean` | `true` | When false renders `children` |
| `children` | `ReactNode` | - | Content shown when `visible` is false |
| `style` | `ViewStyle` | - | Style override |
| `duration` / `delay` / `performanceMode` / `priority` | - | - | **Deprecated no-ops** (kept for backward compatibility; the shared clock makes them unnecessary) |

## Performance notes

- One shimmer loop for the whole app, regardless of skeleton count.
- Pulse animates only opacity; no layout-affecting properties.
- No global animation cap — every skeleton always shimmers, in sync.
